            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Jinu,\n\nRecently I've started asking that new APIs also add a fuzz test:\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/libpldm/blob/8bfb20aa3d82cf892a50eef3258819c6170a6e0b/CONTRIBUTING.md#L269\n\nBefore we stabilise these, can you please do so (in a separate commit as a parent of this one)?\n\nThe fuzz implementation is here:\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/libpldm/blob/main/tests/fuzz/fuzz.c\n\nThe implementation should use the decoder and the `foreach_*()` macros you've added for the state effecter PDR.\n\nLet me know if you have questions."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Apologies Jino, I realise I made an error with your name there."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JINO ABRAHAM",
                        "email": "jinoabraham26@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Jino26"
                    },
                    "message": "No worries. I have a few queries regarding the fuzz tests:\n1. Can I include these fuzz tests within the same ```fuzz.c``` file, or do I need to create a new file?\n2. The ```foreach_*()``` macros internally invoke the decode functions (unless init or other checks fail). However, do you want me to add separate fuzz tests for the decode methods? And also I hope a single fuzz test would be sufficient for covering both foreach macros.\n3. For the state effecter PDR, do you want the whole fuzz input treated as the raw PDR buffer, or a prefixed layout (e.g., a leading length, then the PDR bytes) so the fuzzer can vary pdr_size independently of the buffer contents?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "> Can I include these fuzz tests within the same fuzz.c file, or do I need to create a new file?\n\nYes, for now, please include your fuzz test(s) in the same file. I plan to split it up in the future when it starts getting unwieldy.\n\n> The foreach_*() macros internally invoke the decode functions (unless init or other checks fail). However, do you want me to add separate fuzz tests for the decode methods? And also I hope a single fuzz test would be sufficient for covering both foreach macros.\n\nA single fuzz test please. One that operates as if you were using the APIs in e.g. pldmd.\n\n> For the state effecter PDR, do you want the whole fuzz input treated as the raw PDR buffer, or a prefixed layout (e.g., a leading length, then the PDR bytes) so the fuzzer can vary pdr_size independently of the buffer contents?\n\nlibfuzzer will vary the buffer lengths regardless. It's fine to use the content directly, though you will need to be careful about padding and alignment. Avoid casting. Use the msgbuf APIs to populate any relevant structs or extract parameters from the input buffer as you see fit.\n\nThe following might be instructive:\n\n- https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/libpldm/+/85298/23/tests/fuzz/fuzz.c\n- https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/libpldm/+/90357/1/tests/fuzz/fuzz.c"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JINO ABRAHAM",
                        "email": "jinoabraham26@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Jino26"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks. I've created another commit with fuzz test as suggested: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/libpldm/+/90413"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Awesome, thanks!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "CHANGELOG.md",
                    "line": 57,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "This should go in the `### Changed` section."
                },
                {
                    "file": "CHANGELOG.md",
                    "line": 57,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JINO ABRAHAM",
